## SQ-TSK-02 | tomato vines climb treated sticks
@group A
@commands FD tomato vine on farmland with `creativedelight:treated_stick` two above, `/gamerule randomTickSpeed 300`; repeat with `supplementaries:stick_tomatoes` under a treated stick
@pass the vine climbs into `creativedelight:treated_stick_tomatoes`, stops at three high
@fails `TomatoClimbTreatedStickMixin` / `SuppTomatoClimbTreatedStickMixin`
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> setblock -10 -61 30 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock -10 -60 30 farmersdelight:tomatoes[age=3]
> setblock -10 -59 30 creativedelight:treated_stick
> setblock -10 -58 30 creativedelight:treated_stick
> setblock -8 -61 30 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock -8 -60 30 supplementaries:stick_tomatoes
> setblock -8 -59 30 creativedelight:treated_stick
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
sleep 60
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute if block -10 -59 30 creativedelight:treated_stick_tomatoes
> execute if block -10 -57 30 minecraft:air
> execute if block -8 -59 30 creativedelight:treated_stick_tomatoes
count Test passed >= 2
look FD vine climbed into treated_stick_tomatoes, at most three high; Supplementaries stick tomatoes likewise (third Test passed)

## SQ-TSK-03 | broken soil reverts vines; treated stick loot
@group A
@commands break the farmland under a treated-stick vine; `/loot` on a `treated_stick` with all three axes
@pass vines revert to `treated_stick` and drop FD tomato loot; 3 treated sticks
@fails `TreatedStickTomatoBlock` remove path, `TreatedStickBlock.getDrops`
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> kill @e[type=item]
> setblock -10 -61 30 minecraft:air destroy
sleep 2
> execute if block -10 -59 30 creativedelight:treated_stick
> execute positioned -10 -60 30 as @e[type=item,distance=..4] run data get entity @s Item
> kill @e[type=item]
> loot spawn -5 -55 34 mine -5 -60 30 minecraft:wooden_axe
> loot spawn -5 -55 34 mine -5 -60 30 minecraft:iron_axe
> loot spawn -5 -55 34 mine -5 -60 30 minecraft:netherite_axe
look vine reverted to treated_stick and dropped FD tomato loot; each axe loot = 1 treated stick (3 total)

## SQ-DM-03 | dandelion maturing: fertile soil about twice as fast as rich soil
@group A
@commands Dandelions on Rich Soil and Fertile Soil, `/gamerule randomTickSpeed 300`
@pass Fertile Soil matures about twice as fast as Rich Soil (`fertileSoilTicks = 10`, `richSoilTicks = 20`)
@fails the config file still holds the old values
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> fill 20 -61 30 29 -61 30 farmersdelight:rich_soil
> fill 20 -61 32 29 -61 32 creativedelight:fertile_soil
> fill 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 minecraft:dandelion
> fill 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 minecraft:dandelion
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 30
sleep 30
> zq count 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> zq count 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
sleep 30
> zq count 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> zq count 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
look fertile row (z 32) matures about twice as fast as rich row (z 30); fertile soil id may differ (record the fill error if any)

